This article is a **draft**, so it only shows up on your computer while you run the site locally; it never appears on www.ahmed-shaker.com. Keep it as a reference, or delete it once you're comfortable with the editor.

## Headings build the table of contents

Every *Heading 2* and *Heading 3* you add appears automatically in the "On this page" sidebar, so readers can jump between sections. Use Heading 2 for main sections and Heading 3 for sub-sections.

### Text formatting

You can use **bold**, *italic*, ~~strikethrough~~, `inline code`, and [links](https://www.ahmed-shaker.com). Links to other websites open in a new tab automatically.

## Lists

- Bullet lists for unordered points
- Keep each point short and scannable
- Nest ideas sparingly

1. Numbered lists for steps
2. Or for ranked items
3. Or for sequences

## Callout boxes

{% callout tone="insight" title="Key insight" %}
Use callouts to highlight the one idea you want a busy executive to remember from the article.
{% /callout %}

{% callout tone="tip" %}
Tips work well for practical advice readers can apply immediately.
{% /callout %}

{% callout tone="warning" %}
Warnings flag risks, pitfalls, or common mistakes.
{% /callout %}

