## Code blocks

Choose the language in the code block settings to get syntax highlighting. Readers get a one-click **Copy** button.

```kotlin
@HiltViewModel
class AccountsViewModel @Inject constructor(
    private val repository: AccountsRepository
) : ViewModel() {
    val accounts = repository.observeAccounts()
        .stateIn(viewModelScope, SharingStarted.WhileSubscribed(5_000), emptyList())
}
```

```yaml
apiVersion: argoproj.io/v1alpha1
kind: Application
metadata:
  name: payments-service
spec:
  destination:
    namespace: payments
```

## Tables

| Option | Best for | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Native (Kotlin / Swift) | Deep OS integration | Highest performance |
| Flutter | Fast cross-platform delivery | One codebase for iOS, Android & Web |
| Web | Back-office portals | Responsive layouts |

## Quotes

> A standard blockquote is good for citing someone else's words or a source.

## Images and videos

Use the image button in the editor toolbar to upload an image; it's stored with the article automatically. To embed a video, insert the **YouTube video** block and paste the link.

---

## Publishing checklist

1. Write a clear **Summary**: it's what people see on LinkedIn, WhatsApp, and Google.
2. Add a **cover image** (1600×840) for the best share previews.
3. Pick a **category** and 3–5 **tags**.
4. Untick **Draft** and click **Save**. The article goes live after the site redeploys (about 1–2 minutes).
5. Open the article and use the share buttons to post it on LinkedIn and elsewhere.
